# === dsh-deepartments patch: pi-ai openai-completions tool-pairing guard (stages 1+2) ===
#
# WHAT THIS FIXES
#   Every turn of an affected session died at step 1 with
#   400 "Messages with role 'tool' must be a response to a preceding message with
#   'tool_calls'" (upstream = Vercel AI Gateway -> deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash,
#   reached through the local key-pooler at 127.0.0.1:4097).
#   Two wire shapes are rejected, and BOTH are produced above this layer:
#     (1) ORPHAN — a `tool` message whose id no preceding assistant issued.
#     (2) INTERLEAVED/DUPLICATE — a `tool` message that does not follow its issuing
#         assistant consecutively, or that answers an already-answered id.
#   LIVE EVIDENCE (host session 15f80d86, 2026-09-22): shape (2). The mailbox/journal
#   delivery of a `dept_sleep` close lands a user message BETWEEN the assistant's
#   tool_calls (seq 7051) and its tool result (seq 7054):
#       assistant(tool_call dept_sleep) -> user(memo) -> user(tool-result)
#   transformMessages' second pass then synthesizes a "No result provided" answer
#   BEFORE that user message, so the real result is emitted afterwards as a
#   duplicate, non-consecutive `tool` message. Because the poisoned pair stays in
#   the model-visible surface, EVERY later turn fails at step 1 until a compaction
#   shadows it (observed windows t64-t127 and t268-t289).
#
# WHAT IT DOES
#   Mirrors the org's proven deepseek-serializer defence
#   (dsh-llm-deepseek-orphan-sweep.patch + dsh-llm-deepseek-toolcall-strip.patch)
#   at the only point that still knows what the request actually carries: the wire
#   list built by convertMessages. A post-pass (__dshGuardToolPairing):
#     - keeps clean transcripts BYTE-IDENTICAL (verified: clean case unchanged);
#     - drops a `tool` message that is orphan, interleaved or duplicate;
#     - strips `tool_calls` (text/reasoning kept) from an assistant whose calls have
#       no complete CONSECUTIVE response, so it cannot trip the opposite 400
#       ("insufficient tool messages following tool_calls");
#     - reports findings on stderr ([dsh-guard-toolpair] ... journald) and appends
#       them to /tmp/dsh-wire-guard/guard.jsonl. Never throws.
#
# TARGET FILE (0.1.5-rc.2 tree)
#   <tree>/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-ai/dist/api/openai-completions.js
#
# FINGERPRINTS (md5)
#   6516b02e157bf51549de615a9f9854a0  pristine (pre-patch backup)
#   3414299222fd13caeb1c8cb38c251044  patched
#   Backup: /opt/dsh/dev-fix-20260917/openai-completions.js.bak-20260922-pre-toolpair-guard
#   Offline verification: /tmp/guard-test.mjs (5/5 contract cases, clean case byte-identical)
#
# WHY NOT UPSTREAM
#   Owner decision (same as the deepseek stages 1+2): folded as a repo patch, lives
#   in the installed tree and is LOST on every dsh upgrade -> re-apply after upgrades.
#
# NOTE — this guard is a WIRE-VALIDITY backstop, not the root-cause fix. The producer
# bug is the mailbox/journal delivery interleaving a pending tool result on the
# dept_sleep close path; that belongs in the deepartments plugin (deliver mailbox
# items only at turn boundaries, or after every pending tool result is recorded).
